<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ismail Qemali</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1844–1919</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Ismail Kemal Bey</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ismail Qemali was an Albanian statesman from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlore">Vlorë</a> who had served as an Ottoman official and liberal deputy. On 28 November 1912, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-balkan-war">First Balkan War</a>, he declared Albania's independence at Vlorë and headed its provisional government. With little army, money or recognition, he resigned in 1914 and is honoured as the founder of modern Albania.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ismail-qemali.jpg" alt="Ismail Qemali" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ismail_Kemal_Bey.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
